  "notes": "DRAFT by Claude (s347) for Ben to move in the Map Workshop. KUFA = a hot DESERT CARAVAN TOWN at the edge of the dry. A square sandstone town: the TOWN SQUARE (K crest, tally board, standpipe, caravan gate) sits on the crossing of CARAVAN WAY (east-west, the caravans' road right through town) and CREST STREET (north-south). The five brief shops + post, bank and watch face the square. WEST: the covered BAZAAR souk (stalls, Ummi's dead-end Camel Pen, Dominoes Club) → the CARAVAN ROAD out through the dunes → the FAR LEG (the Siphon rig) → THE WAY STATION → THE BERTH. NORTH: Castle Path over the dry WADI (bridge) to Emir Tahir's hall + the Barracks. SOUTH: THE OASIS (the only lake: dock, skiff dive to Station 9), the date-palm Fox Farm and the Sand Dock. EAST: Stadium Path fork → the Kufa Stadium. Everything else is open DUNE SEA (off-path freedom, creatures live out there). Palms come from terrain.forests mix 'palm' (new s347). NPC keys are draft until surface_kufa.html comes in. EVERY BUILDING IS UNIQUE (Ben, s348): each building has an \"outside\" note = its own shape, roof and landmark detail for phase 2. No two share a design.",
